# Rules

## HTML Rules

1. Use semantic HTML elements (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`, `aside`, `footer`) instead of generic `div`/`span` where appropriate
2. Do not use inline styles (`style` attribute) – separate presentation into CSS
3. Validate HTML to avoid unclosed tags, duplicate attributes, or invalid nesting
4. Separate homogeneous tags with an empty line

## CSS Rules

1. Use class names for styling; avoid ID selectors for styling
2. Follow a consistent BEM naming methodology
3. Avoid `!important`
4. Use CSS Flexbox and Grid
5. Keep selectors shallow – maximum 3 levels of nesting
6. Group related CSS rules logically and remove unused styles

## Code Organization

1. Keep CSS in separate `.css` files
2. Do not use CSS-in-JS approach
3. Name CSS files consistently with their component/page name (e.g., `Header.css` or `Header.module.css`)
4. Use CSS custom properties (variables) for theming and repeated values (colors, spacing, typography)
5. Use 2-space indentation – be consistent across the project
6. Remove dead code: regularly audit and delete unused HTML elements and CSS rules